  clock: 3  # 9f52
  nonce: 9f52  # 9f52
  message: "DONE -- PR #735 (23c768b6b4, rebase-merged 2026-09-03 07:35Z). Behavioural evidence, the item's own filed repro re-run on\nthe fixed tree against the live CI:\n\n  $ ./scripts/ci-debug logs self-claims-gate 8955d9a2\n  Fetching CI log for commit 8955d9a2 (job: self-claims-gate)...\n  + pip install --upgrade pip && pip install jsonschema\n  ... (485 lines, the cron/full-suite pipeline 2206 step) ...\n  + PYTHON=python scripts/check-self-claims\n  check-self-claims: analysing hypergumbo with hypergumbo ...\n  check-self-claims-drift: OK -- 18 claims unchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats).\n\nNo \"Nothing named\" / \"INSTEAD\" line: the step was found on the second gate\nand fetched from its pipeline. Before the fix the same command printed the\npush pipeline's apt-get + pytest transcript behind the substitution warning.\n\nMECHANISM confirmed from the fetcher's own WI-zavut comment: gate selection\nby context, then fallback to the failed/first gate, BEFORE any step is\nconsulted -- so a step name on a sibling gate always lost. Fix: when the\nname matches no gate, search every gate's pipeline for the step (failed\nfirst) and let the first hit choose the pipeline; the honest fallback\nsurvives for the genuinely-absent case, pinned by a control test that\nasserts both pipelines were read before the warning.\n\nHarness drift fixed alongside (fake curl printed the code alone without -o;\nnow body then code for -w, as real curl and the sibling fake do); 72 tests\nacross nine harness consumers pass.\n\nThis also supplies the transcript INV-bofab's satisfied note recorded as\nunread; a discussion entry there points here."  # 9f52
